  "description": "UVOKUP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C119 H97 Eu3 O41 Ti5. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti4 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti5 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.347-4.287 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.86-142.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu3Ti5(μ2-O)(μ3-O)5(BA)15(THF)(acac)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ2-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
